WEBVTT

00:03.750 --> 00:05.630
<b>Well, time to get cracking.</b>

00:08.170 --> 00:09.880
<b>Sic 'im, boys.</b>

00:26.000 --> 00:31.580
<b>Impressive swordsmanship. But you're gonna
have to do better than that to beat my inugami.</b>

00:53.330 --> 00:54.670
<b>There's just no end to them.</b>

00:56.170 --> 00:57.330
<b>Invisibility.</b>

00:59.710 --> 01:01.920
<b>Oh! So that's your power?</b>

01:12.170 --> 01:15.210
<b>Didn'tcha know? Dogs have very keen senses.</b>

01:24.130 --> 01:26.670
<b>It's too bad that your power turned out to be useless!</b>

01:26.920 --> 01:30.080
<b>Indeed. Which means it's time for plan B.</b>

01:30.420 --> 01:31.080
<b>Hm?</b>

01:31.580 --> 01:32.540
<b>Dart.</b>

03:18.250 --> 03:19.960
<b>Yeowch, that hurt!</b>

03:22.380 --> 03:25.040
<b>Say, buddy. Why do you have two pow-?</b>

03:30.130 --> 03:31.790
<b>Hold your horses!</b>

03:36.920 --> 03:40.080
<b>Nice try, but you missed. I'm just a mirage.</b>

03:47.750 --> 03:50.380
<b>Sorry, buddy. But this is the end of the line.</b>

03:52.750 --> 03:55.500
<b>My inugami are pretty amazing, don'tcha think?</b>

03:55.960 --> 03:57.830
<b>Oh, shoot. You can't hear me anymore, huh?</b>

04:00.420 --> 04:01.330
<b>Toodle-oo.</b>

04:02.880 --> 04:05.130
<b>I'll admit, they were rather formidable.</b>

04:08.630 --> 04:10.210
<b>How are you not dead?</b>

04:10.540 --> 04:15.130
<b>I'm honestly impressed.
Your dog spirits are on par with superior demons.</b>

04:16.460 --> 04:18.210
<b>Attack, inugami!</b>

04:24.790 --> 04:26.170
<b>You stole them from me?!</b>

04:26.420 --> 04:28.170
<b>Aw, man! That's not fair!</b>

04:33.210 --> 04:34.540
<b>Have mercy.</b>

04:34.540 --> 04:35.750
<b>Why should I?</b>

04:36.460 --> 04:39.170
<b>Now talk. Let's hear what you have to say.</b>

04:39.920 --> 04:41.210
<b>You're not gonna kill me?</b>

04:41.380 --> 04:45.580
<b>I need you to answer some questions.
I won't kill you if you agree to talk.</b>

04:45.960 --> 04:47.630
<b>And if I refuse?</b>

04:48.580 --> 04:51.250
<b>Then I'll just have to steal your memories
by consuming you.</b>

04:51.670 --> 04:52.630
<b>Yikes.</b>

04:52.960 --> 04:55.880
<b>Alrighty, then. I guess I'll answer your questions.</b>

04:56.130 --> 04:58.670
<b>Not like I can fight back, anyway.</b>

04:58.670 --> 05:02.960
<b>Yeah, right. I know you must
still have tricks up your sleeve.</b>

05:03.250 --> 05:07.210
<b>Look who's talking.
You held back your own powers, didn'tcha?</b>

05:09.500 --> 05:13.750
<b>I'll happily answer your questions.
But would you get rid of these pups first?</b>

05:13.880 --> 05:15.580
<b>They're freaking me out.</b>

05:24.420 --> 05:28.330
<b>You really did it! Has anybody told you
that you're way too gullible?</b>

05:28.790 --> 05:30.580
<b>You're not lying though, are you?</b>

05:30.670 --> 05:31.630
<b>Other people do.</b>

05:32.130 --> 05:35.710
<b>Can you give me just a sec? I've gotta fetch my inugami.</b>

05:36.080 --> 05:39.880
<b>Oh, but don't worry. I won't try and make a break for it.</b>

05:45.000 --> 05:48.920
<b>Thanks, boys. I'll be sure to put you to rest later.</b>

05:50.960 --> 05:51.880
<b>What're those?</b>

05:52.630 --> 05:54.420
<b>Papier-mache figurines.</b>

05:54.830 --> 05:58.790
<b>Have you ever heard of "tsukumogami"?
Basically, they're objects infused with emotion.</b>

05:59.420 --> 06:00.830
<b>And feelings are power.</b>

06:01.290 --> 06:04.170
<b>Since negative emotions
can become demons with bodies of flesh,</b>

06:04.500 --> 06:08.130
<b>it's not farfetched for objects to come to life, too, right?</b>

06:08.580 --> 06:12.960
<b>In other words, you can take the emotions
of objects and turn them into demons?</b>

06:13.250 --> 06:16.080
<b>Exactly. I can create tsukumogami.</b>

06:16.330 --> 06:21.380
<b>I'm like one of those spirit mediums who controls
magical familiars, just with tsukumogami instead.</b>

06:21.750 --> 06:25.420
<b>You called yourself the third generation.
Are you from a family of exorcists?</b>

06:25.790 --> 06:27.380
<b>No, not really.</b>

06:27.630 --> 06:31.330
<b>Notable exorcists like Nagumo of the Cursed Sword
and Kukami of the Magatama</b>

06:31.330 --> 06:35.750
<b>inherit their techniques by blood,
but Akitsu is more of a school.</b>

06:36.290 --> 06:39.630
<b>Initially, Somegoro Akitsu was just an ordinary craftsman.</b>

06:40.330 --> 06:43.130
<b>But the thing is, he was too good at it.</b>

06:43.540 --> 06:47.380
<b>Every object that Somegoro created
ended up with a soul of its own.</b>

06:48.000 --> 06:49.080
<b>And I don't mean figuratively.</b>

06:49.790 --> 06:53.210
<b>Things intensified until he conceived
of a technique to turn those objects</b>

06:53.210 --> 06:55.210
<b>into tsukumogami that could be controlled.</b>

06:55.580 --> 07:00.540
<b>After Somegoro retired, he passed on everything
to his disciple and I'm the third one to take the mantle.</b>

07:01.000 --> 07:05.880
<b>But the name "Somegoro Akitsu"
is famous for good craftsmanship, not exorcism.</b>

07:06.670 --> 07:08.290
<b>Sorry, I got off on a tangent.</b>

07:08.670 --> 07:10.170
<b>So, buddy...</b>

07:10.880 --> 07:11.790
<b>It's Jinya.</b>

07:12.130 --> 07:16.250
<b>Right. So, what did you want to ask me, Jinya-san?</b>

07:16.540 --> 07:19.830
<b>Yesterday, you sold a kanzashi to a young lady, yes?</b>

07:19.920 --> 07:23.330
<b>A kanzashi? Yesterday? Let me think...</b>

07:24.080 --> 07:27.750
<b>Ah! That wasn't really a sale,
but yes, I did give one away.</b>

07:28.210 --> 07:32.080
<b>Well, the instant she put it on, that young lady
took on a totally different personality.</b>

07:32.830 --> 07:34.500
<b>What's the deal with that kanzashi?</b>

07:34.670 --> 07:38.830
<b>I'm not sure what to tell you.
It was just an ordinary hairpin.</b>

07:41.630 --> 07:43.250
<b>Oh, hey! I've got it!</b>

07:44.920 --> 07:47.420
<b>I think I can solve your problem with the young lady.</b>

07:47.710 --> 07:50.630
<b>So how about you just put that sword away, okay?</b>

07:51.250 --> 07:52.670
<b>Do you really mean that?</b>

07:53.250 --> 07:54.250
<b>Who knows?</b>

07:54.380 --> 07:57.000
<b>I might be lying, or I might be telling the truth.</b>

07:57.500 --> 08:02.290
<b>But in either case, you have no choice
except to believe me, right?</b>

08:25.880 --> 08:26.540
<b>Natsu.</b>

08:30.830 --> 08:33.290
<b>Welcome home, dear brother.</b>

08:33.670 --> 08:34.830
<b>You were waiting for me?</b>

08:35.130 --> 08:38.170
<b>Yes. Because that's what you asked me to do.</b>

08:38.500 --> 08:40.460
<b>Sorry. I know I'm late.</b>

08:40.920 --> 08:46.000
<b>That's okay. I knew that you
would come back to me eventually.</b>

08:49.710 --> 08:51.290
<b>Let's go out, shall we?</b>

08:51.960 --> 08:55.380
<b>Sure. I'll gladly go anywhere with you, dear brother.</b>

09:08.000 --> 09:12.080
<b>These are snow willows.
They bloom flowers in spring that look like snow.</b>

09:12.380 --> 09:14.130
<b>You're very knowledgeable.</b>

09:16.250 --> 09:17.380
<b>Dear brother?</b>

09:18.130 --> 09:21.710
<b>To be perfectly honest,
I don't handle being called "brother" well.</b>

09:22.710 --> 09:26.630
<b>It makes me feel like my biggest vulnerability
has been exposed and I hate that.</b>

09:27.500 --> 09:29.290
<b>But, dear brother...</b>

09:31.460 --> 09:32.670
<b>I wanted to protect it.</b>

09:33.250 --> 09:35.040
<b>But I wasn't able to.</b>

09:36.380 --> 09:38.080
<b>Not a single thing.</b>

09:39.670 --> 09:43.170
<b>The promise I made on that distant rainy night
got broken so easily,</b>

09:43.540 --> 09:46.630
<b>and I... failed to be her loving brother until the end.</b>

09:50.880 --> 09:52.790
<b>I'm not Jinta anymore.</b>

09:53.460 --> 09:57.330
<b>And ultimately, when it comes to you and to Suzune...</b>

09:57.880 --> 09:59.380
<b>I am no big brother.</b>

10:00.750 --> 10:01.500
<b>Wrong.</b>

10:09.750 --> 10:13.670
<b>Why should a bird need any reason
to perch itself by a flower?</b>

10:14.330 --> 10:16.580
<b>The same is true of siblings, is it not?</b>

10:17.500 --> 10:21.830
<b>No matter what the circumstances,
their bonds can never be completely broken.</b>

10:22.960 --> 10:28.380
<b>After living across many moons,
I finally found my way here to be by your side.</b>

10:29.040 --> 10:34.130
<b>And so, I have no doubt that you can
also find a path that will take you back.</b>

10:34.960 --> 10:35.830
<b>Take me back...?</b>

10:36.250 --> 10:36.880
<b>Yes.</b>

10:37.460 --> 10:44.170
<b>We all live in search of the place where our feelings
call home, which requires a long journey across time.</b>

10:44.710 --> 10:46.210
<b>I doubt I can find that path...</b>

10:46.380 --> 10:51.170
<b>You will. After all, that is the purpose of life.</b>

10:51.630 --> 10:52.460
<b>Natsu...</b>

10:53.130 --> 10:56.580
<b>No, that's not right.
I'm sorry I don't know what to call you.</b>

11:00.830 --> 11:04.460
<b>Thanks for listening to my griping.
I owe you a debt of gratitude.</b>

11:05.960 --> 11:09.460
<b>Here. Let me return your other half.</b>

11:15.130 --> 11:18.290
<b>You've got something in your breast pocket, don'tcha?</b>

11:18.630 --> 11:22.170
<b>If my guess is right, then it's probably a comb or a kogai.</b>

11:22.380 --> 11:24.290
<b>Actually, I'd put my money on a kogai.</b>

11:24.670 --> 11:27.460
<b>Just give it to that girl and your problem is solved.</b>

11:29.210 --> 11:30.420
<b>My dear brother...</b>

11:32.710 --> 11:36.210
<b>After so long, I can reach out and touch you.</b>

11:43.830 --> 11:45.460
<b>A cuckoo bird?</b>

11:46.170 --> 11:47.790
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

11:48.580 --> 11:50.920
<b>Now I have found my place.</b>

11:58.210 --> 11:59.710
<b>Dear brother...</b>

12:05.670 --> 12:07.830
<b>...let us go together.</b>

12:20.500 --> 12:21.880
<b>Congrats.</b>

12:23.880 --> 12:25.210
<b>Somegoro Akitsu.</b>

12:25.580 --> 12:27.790
<b>Yeesh, you really gotta use my full name? Well, whatever.</b>

12:27.790 --> 12:31.290
<b>More importantly, it worked just like I said, right?</b>

12:38.080 --> 12:41.330
<b>The word "kogai" comes
from the kanji for "hair-scratcher."</b>

12:42.500 --> 12:45.500
<b>Originally, it was a tool that people used to style hair,</b>

12:45.750 --> 12:49.210
<b>but also to scratch their itchy heads
without ruining their hairdo,</b>

12:49.500 --> 12:51.920
<b>or by young ladies to keep up their appearance.</b>

12:52.920 --> 12:58.830
<b>So, I suppose if they were made by the same craftsman,
you could think of kogai and kanzashi like family.</b>

12:59.790 --> 13:05.290
<b>Oh, but since kanzashi are for women and kogai
are tools that men keep attached to their swords,</b>

13:05.290 --> 13:07.960
<b>they're more like older brother and little sister.</b>

13:08.880 --> 13:11.540
<b>That wisteria kogai
was another Somegoro work, ya know?</b>

13:12.170 --> 13:17.790
<b>So since you had the sibling piece of that hairpin,
I'm guessing that's why it kept calling you "dear brother."</b>

13:18.790 --> 13:23.420
<b>That kanzashi contained the lingering emotions
of its long departed owner.</b>

13:24.080 --> 13:29.250
<b>Frankly, I thought Natsu was searching for this "dear
brother" because she had gotten possessed by those.</b>

13:29.750 --> 13:33.380
<b>And what? You resemble that brother or something?</b>

13:35.040 --> 13:37.420
<b>It's like a story straight out of a stage play!</b>

13:38.290 --> 13:42.250
<b>But really, it seems like those
two pieces were created as a pair.</b>

13:43.210 --> 13:50.380
<b>"The blooming waves of wisteria come crashing down,
as if to betoken the arrival of the cuckoos call."</b>

13:50.960 --> 13:52.790
<b>That's a poem from the man'yoshu.</b>

13:52.790 --> 13:55.290
<b>Somegoro the First was quite the jokester.</b>

13:56.170 --> 14:00.210
<b>Why should a bird need any reason
to perch itself by a flower?</b>

14:01.420 --> 14:06.330
<b>So you're telling me that cuckoo hairpin
was searching for wisteria flowers all along, huh?</b>

14:07.080 --> 14:09.580
<b>Strange things really do happen in life.</b>

14:10.000 --> 14:11.830
<b>That's weird for a demon to say.</b>

14:12.880 --> 14:16.630
<b>In any case, the journey that kanzashi took is a mystery,</b>

14:17.130 --> 14:19.920
<b>since nobody can really know whose hands it passed
between to fill it with such emotion,</b>

14:20.130 --> 14:23.380
<b>and we don't need to know, anyway.</b>

14:23.880 --> 14:27.880
<b>The only thing that matters is the cuckoo
found its way back to its brother.</b>

14:28.630 --> 14:30.040
<b>All's well that ends well.</b>

14:33.380 --> 14:35.380
<b>Where do you suppose it flew off to?</b>

14:36.000 --> 14:37.960
<b>Into the yonder, obviously.</b>

14:38.330 --> 14:39.210
<b>Yonder?</b>

14:39.380 --> 14:43.210
<b>Yep. Beyond the seas and into the distant skies.</b>

14:43.540 --> 14:47.080
<b>Far, far away. To where its feelings call home.</b>

14:47.580 --> 14:51.210
<b>The only way to know exactly where is to ask the cuckoo.</b>

14:51.880 --> 14:57.460
<b>But at any rate, emotions always return to the place
they desire most in the end. That's what I believe.</b>

14:59.210 --> 15:00.130
<b>I see.</b>

15:01.960 --> 15:03.210
<b>I hope that's the case.</b>

15:06.130 --> 15:09.290
<b>Alrighty, then. I better get going.</b>

15:09.790 --> 15:12.290
<b>I suppose I should ask. You're letting me go?</b>

15:12.750 --> 15:13.460
<b>What do you mean?</b>

15:14.420 --> 15:16.540
<b>I'm a demon disguised as a human.</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.580
<b>Oh, is that all?</b>

15:18.880 --> 15:20.710
<b>Meh, I'm okay with it.</b>

15:22.920 --> 15:27.630
<b>Don't be such a stiff! I mean,
you're friends with Ofuu-chan, aren'tcha?</b>

15:27.920 --> 15:30.630
<b>Too late for me to change course
after I let her off the hook,</b>

15:30.790 --> 15:32.960
<b>and you don't seem dangerous, anyways.</b>

15:33.460 --> 15:34.080
<b>But...</b>

15:34.330 --> 15:36.040
<b>I'm just a craftsman at the end of the day.</b>

15:36.380 --> 15:40.670
<b>I do slay demons upon request,
and will fight back when threatened,</b>

15:41.000 --> 15:43.830
<b>but I'm not out to kill demons that mean no harm.</b>

15:44.960 --> 15:47.500
<b>That said, you'd better not forget.</b>

15:47.960 --> 15:52.750
<b>Y'all are demons, which means
you're always gonna be on the side that gets hunted.</b>

15:54.540 --> 16:00.580
<b>No matter how kind Ofuu-chan is, or how many people
you've saved, or how close y'all are with humans like me,</b>

16:00.960 --> 16:02.210
<b>that fact will never change.</b>

16:04.170 --> 16:05.130
<b>I'm aware.</b>

16:05.830 --> 16:07.290
<b>Glad to hear it.</b>

16:07.790 --> 16:09.250
<b>Well, toodle-oo!</b>

16:16.920 --> 16:20.500
<b>Whew! It's such a relief that you're back to normal!</b>

16:21.040 --> 16:22.170
<b>Except...</b>

16:22.460 --> 16:25.420
<b>Why are so you down in the dumps about it, milady?</b>

16:25.630 --> 16:30.130
<b>Well, you see, she has clear memories
of everything that happened.</b>

16:30.580 --> 16:31.960
<b>Oh, dang.</b>

16:31.960 --> 16:35.130
<b>Like, "dear brother" and all that other sappy talk
she pampered him with?</b>

16:35.290 --> 16:37.130
<b>That would turn anybody red in the face.</b>

16:37.460 --> 16:40.330
<b>Zenji! You're just asking for trouble!</b>

16:40.580 --> 16:43.290
<b>Oh, sorry! I wasn't trying to make fun of you.</b>

16:43.290 --> 16:45.540
<b>Shucks. Just simmer down, Natsu-chan.</b>

16:46.080 --> 16:49.380
<b>Go ahead and order whatever you want.
It's on the house.</b>

16:49.380 --> 16:52.080
<b>Aw, thanks, Mister!</b>

16:53.210 --> 16:55.460
<b>But I notice that our ronin friend hasn't shown up today.</b>

16:56.750 --> 16:58.630
<b>Ready to turn into a clam yet?</b>

16:59.710 --> 17:03.830
<b>You know... I think I'm happy just being a sparrow.</b>

17:04.170 --> 17:05.250
<b>My, my.</b>

17:06.880 --> 17:11.040
<b>Aw, jeez! How am I
supposed to look him in the face now?</b>

17:18.250 --> 17:21.210
<b>Goodness. You've got quite the frown today.</b>

17:22.080 --> 17:26.130
<b>Harlot. A little early to be prowling for men, isn't it?</b>

17:26.460 --> 17:31.330
<b>Here I was trying to show a little concern,
and all you can be is rude?</b>

17:31.830 --> 17:34.790
<b>Well, since you're here, care to chat for a bit?</b>

17:35.130 --> 17:37.630
<b>The rumor mill has been churning lately.</b>

17:38.080 --> 17:39.290
<b>I'd love to hear more.</b>

17:41.500 --> 17:45.670
<b>I take it you're in the mood for some action
to clear your mind, huh?</b>

17:48.500 --> 17:49.630
<b>Did you hear that?</b>

17:49.750 --> 17:51.710
<b>Ugh, not again.</b>

17:52.630 --> 17:58.580
<b>Actually, earlier this morning, I was trying to sleep
when I heard the call of a cuckoo from somewhere.</b>

17:59.000 --> 18:02.290
<b>It was so noisy that I couldn't sleep,
which is why I'm out and about.</b>

18:02.460 --> 18:08.290
<b>But even now, I just keep hearing
its cry nearby. It's so strange.</b>

18:09.210 --> 18:11.080
<b>Hm? What is it?</b>

18:12.000 --> 18:16.960
<b>Emotions always return to the place they desire most
in the end. That's what I believe.</b>

18:17.580 --> 18:19.580
<b>There's just no way...</b>

18:19.710 --> 18:21.380
<b>C'mon, what's the deal?</b>

18:21.830 --> 18:24.500
<b>Wait. You don't suppose it's a demon, do you?</b>

18:25.540 --> 18:26.420
<b>No.</b>

18:26.750 --> 18:31.170
<b>Just a cuckoo that made its way through the night,
and found a flower to perch next to.</b>

18:36.540 --> 18:40.830
<b>As time stretches on further and further,
neither people nor nature can defy it.</b>

18:45.210 --> 18:47.380
<b>Nothing is forever.</b>

18:48.040 --> 18:53.130
<b>However, there is one exception. Human emotions.</b>

18:54.170 --> 18:56.750
<b>No matter what new shape they may take on...</b>

18:54.710 --> 18:58.290
<b>HEISEI YEAR 21 (2009)</b>

18:58.790 --> 19:01.960
<b>That looks great on you, Miyaka-chan!</b>

19:03.380 --> 19:04.670
<b>Jeez, Mom.</b>

19:04.960 --> 19:05.710
<b>What?</b>

19:06.080 --> 19:10.710
<b>It's been bothering me forever,
but why do you insist on making me do this Miko thing?</b>

19:11.250 --> 19:16.460
<b>Like this outfit... I'd be totally mortified
if a friend of mine showed up right now.</b>

19:16.920 --> 19:23.080
<b>Good question. I suppose it's because
that's the duty of the women who are born at this shrine.</b>

19:23.630 --> 19:27.960
<b>I was given two rules: one to add the "night" kanji
to my daughter's name.</b>

19:28.290 --> 19:31.130
<b>And the other to never let the Miko line die out.</b>

19:31.460 --> 19:35.500
<b>My grandmother insisted that we keep
those traditions alive no matter what,</b>

19:35.500 --> 19:38.710
<b>so I have to pass them down to future generations.</b>

19:39.080 --> 19:39.920
<b>But why?</b>

19:40.170 --> 19:41.130
<b>Who knows?</b>

19:41.460 --> 19:42.880
<b>You can't be serious.</b>

19:43.670 --> 19:45.710
<b>Even if we don't know the reasons,</b>

19:45.830 --> 19:51.710
<b>these traditions must be incredibly significant
to whoever originally made them.</b>

19:52.420 --> 19:54.290
<b>So I feel obligated to uphold them.</b>

19:54.880 --> 20:01.880
<b>Of course, the most important part aren't the
traditions themselves, but the feelings they represent.</b>

20:02.920 --> 20:06.130
<b>Which is why the ladies of our family
all have "ya" in our names.</b>

20:06.710 --> 20:12.210
<b>The sentiments from those ages long ago
may have gotten lost in the passage of time,</b>

20:12.630 --> 20:15.750
<b>but they still have a home to come back to.</b>

20:17.710 --> 20:20.080
<b>And now, it's your turn to make sure the feelings</b>

20:20.080 --> 20:23.380
<b>of those people from the past
can endure into the future, Miyaka-chan.</b>

20:27.040 --> 20:30.500
<b>Okay, I better start fixing dinner now.</b>

20:34.790 --> 20:36.170
<b>She's so weird...</b>

20:37.330 --> 20:41.000
<b>Brr, it's cold! I gotta wrap this up quick.</b>

20:45.710 --> 20:46.670
<b>Pardon me.</b>

20:47.210 --> 20:47.790
<b>Yes?</b>

20:48.960 --> 20:53.130
<b>Are you the Miko of this shrine?
I'd like to ask you something.</b>

20:53.630 --> 20:56.790
<b>Sort of. We're called Itsukihime instead of Miko.</b>

20:57.290 --> 20:58.830
<b>Itsukihime...?</b>

20:59.290 --> 21:02.170
<b>I don't know the exact reason why,</b>

21:02.380 --> 21:06.960
<b>but it's always been a rule here
at the Jinta Shrine to call the Miko by that title.</b>

21:07.330 --> 21:11.880
<b>I'm sorry. But could you repeat
the name of this shrine for me?</b>

21:12.170 --> 21:14.960
<b>Sure. It's called Jinta shrine.</b>

21:16.830 --> 21:18.710
<b>I see...</b>

21:22.130 --> 21:26.670
<b>Thanks, chieftain... you came through on your promise
to make sure this shrine endured,</b>

21:26.670 --> 21:28.630
<b>so I had a place to come back to.</b>

21:30.630 --> 21:33.750
<b>Thank you very much. Now, if you'll excuse me.</b>

21:34.040 --> 21:36.420
<b>Huh? Didn't you have a question for me?</b>

21:38.250 --> 21:39.460
<b>You've already answered it.</b>

21:39.880 --> 21:43.750
<b>You delivered exactly the words
that I was hoping to hear.</b>

21:45.920 --> 21:48.250
<b>JINTA SHRINE</b>

21:51.710 --> 21:53.710
<b>ENTRANCE CEREMONY</b>

21:53.710 --> 21:56.420
<b>CLASS 1-C ROSTER</b>

21:53.710 --> 21:56.420
<b>JINYA KADONO</b>

21:53.710 --> 21:56.420
<b>MIYAKA HIMEKAWA</b>

21:55.130 --> 21:56.420
<b>Yahoo!</b>

21:56.580 --> 21:58.750
<b>We're in the same class! This is awesome!</b>

21:58.750 --> 21:59.830
<b>Talk about lucky, Miyaka-chan!</b>

21:59.830 --> 22:00.920
<b>I'm so happy, Kaoru-chan!</b>

22:00.920 --> 22:02.500
<b>Same!</b>
